+# Free-Text Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope, Specialty Narrowing Does Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian in one row, on the ground that owner search already demonstrates paged prefix search and repeating it elsewhere adds surface without adding understanding. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey.
+
+The owner has now asked for the veterinarian directory to be narrowable to one specialty (2026-08-23). That request meets NG-9 head-on: read at full width, the row forbids it. Read for its rationale, the row forbids re-teaching prefix search over free text, which narrowing by a specialty the directory already prints does not do.
+
+A row that a request can reopen by implication is not a boundary. The row is therefore decided rather than left to interpretation.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 at full width.** Refuse the request. Rejected: the rationale does not reach the case. The specialty is an attribute the directory already shows, and narrowing by it repeats no pattern the sample teaches elsewhere.
+2. **Retire NG-9.** Open veterinarian search generally. Rejected: this discards a boundary the request never challenged. Free-text veterinarian search would be a second paged prefix search, which is exactly what the row declined.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 covers free-text search only. Narrowing a published list to one exact value of an attribute that list already shows is outside it, and `REQ-VET-004` is that narrowing for the veterinarian directory.
+
+Pets and visits are untouched: neither is searchable and neither is narrowable, because neither is published as a list to narrow.
+
+`REQ-VET-004` is bounded to the request contract. Neither published form of the directory gains a form, a dropdown, or any other page control in this scope. A visible control is a separate request, recorded as an open question rather than implied by this one.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation as a decided row. Every row other than NG-4, NG-5, and NG-9 remains part of it.
+- Matching on the whole specialty name, not a prefix, is the load-bearing line between this capability and the row. A prefix match would rebuild the declined search.
+- A later request to narrow another published list by an attribute it shows is in scope by this decision. A request to search any entity by typed-in text is not, and needs its own owner decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the amended preamble.
+- [REQ-VET-004](../prd.md#req-vet-004) — the capability the narrowing admits.
